{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0eb128f3673858b61ac29b3ec092b37a95ce3fb8ae2d00f54822e11cd41a6aef","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c9b4f9e258f86e86763df096f2466bc34d4609d5f8354bb1e55995ef6b7e903b"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"The agent manages background tasks with configurable wait timeout and a concurrency cap (default 32, up to 64), and bash commands detach after a default 2-minute timeout with a SIGTERM-to-SIGKILL grace period.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0f36525f32f17b453ee4879d1d93804220d1cbd4626418aa397337225ec83e72","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b4811475a2d14e1b7571aa74c4276b5a7b04d84bd4b739c2b47e6466c2a8acf5"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"The CLI supports an interactive REPL, one-shot `-p` prompts (including stdin input), `-c` to continue the latest session, and `--resume`/`--resume=ID` session selection.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_30bcf644ee94d3af4f80a09281ab902a760de0c5d924057511c412a6f0240cb9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1722f87bf15c540318bf9b0f40cc9e243d6c0e3c9d60f3f72dd7c35b4abd472f","slc_28167ef9cc76f89c28e01a969929d5c21b8d55c14272780730f6c43d771340fa","slc_820f7147d255d9516d27b9247e9e1445b1347895120d8abef5a84a9d8737e173","slc_8fc22029fcfa9f4c922a2506504dc51a1bd223cfe13ba86b197eef3dab0fab66","slc_9bc52fdb6e763c2bd0136ddd341a7d07c3f291a7a462df272ab77604655c2fa4","slc_ebe2e0ce07f800daa8128fdc7cda0fda92fa17ec7362dc74a63d6ab3b521143e"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e","src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59","src_c221790ae46f514eade2e02dc420ed4c"],"text":"In the REPL, slash commands such as `/provider`, `/model`, `/effort`, `/preset`, `/config`, and `/preset-save` select providers and settings; Ctrl-T opens a transcript view in $PAGER and Ctrl-O shows the conversation as displayed.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_362da9659487f20a7268af2e770bc0e5fa0d6edf7fced28afd16b535c1ef1db2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb37cc9788c9d5b477d30d972ce0c8861c565b4417eaf5bef9a2528ad2663d4b","slc_c9b4f9e258f86e86763df096f2466bc34d4609d5f8354bb1e55995ef6b7e903b"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e","src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"The bash tool runs commands through a configurable shell with a default 2-minute timeout before detaching; the maximum timeout a model may request defaults to 30 minutes, and no per-command permission prompts exist by design.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5b48e394d74fd4fa22e8c34b1d56a86245e86f2f59566d205b05e13fb73bab0d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_47b42e2a8a13169d0be3eed51850e926559b54c60cd13a383a1228422a08e972","slc_9c7afb082be3ff0ce902fa9f400cf83ee70e6750e10da828a6369bf302ba3db2"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"Presets can act as roles with description, system-prompt additions, and a tint; only presets with a description are advertised to the model as subagent delegation targets.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_63e789213d56068885577357f057d841d23bb86aa233dcce102425a6838d7f49","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_580402cfbceac83ef4658c1f91ede2c07555b25fc46989564422f4fd5a4e4d56"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"The product runs on Linux, macOS, FreeBSD, and OpenBSD; on Windows it is used under WSL, and the BSDs are build-from-source only.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_643e2a0ab2ba1350b992425809e4d12e3230d8b478ae6c689b84a7e507d5b08c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10d1192b15abbff3e78cff976d96329fdb4fdb30601c4ff484132b437bf2c15e","slc_1dcc1712c2fee67712dde3de4e8a6cc2ae6dddd1551a6a2754de4f7b6694b283","slc_5ba87ba8e238027b9daa0e4aca54c27df206eae29bd9896d92d3ee23625fde60","slc_855246463bd2e6c754f40686b476843d8fad20b51dd47ba256a9079f781a20bd"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59","src_c221790ae46f514eade2e02dc420ed4c"],"text":"A wire-protocol trace can be collected via HAX_TRACE, capturing HTTP requests, statuses, and SSE events with credentials redacted; HAX_TRANSCRIPT mirrors the model-facing transcript to a file.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6b6385776d48222ef924641d5e9da65f1842e55b08ac8557f774829c385966c9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14ba78477875cfbac13edda64236ee75be1a4439560524ed5313f20196d7f158","slc_454530ca32d42eb84173584aed4549918ac0cfcd8bba5e5461e8c59352ac2c37"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e","src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"Provider support includes OpenAI and compatible endpoints, Anthropic and compatible endpoints, Codex via ChatGPT login, OpenRouter, OpenCode Zen/Go, llama.cpp, ollama, and custom endpoints configured through providers.<id> blocks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_87b02669371e24fa28b69b6621de571692886c9c379d2e014c867058acb9e174","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_442b6a0e8bce1858dc9b2c631e344129a8dd759c690a6fac8d7656a963b129dc"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"Building from source requires a C compiler, libcurl, jansson, meson, ninja, and pkg-config; fzf is additionally used for @file completion when available.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_97e1694f9ea8308f67ad197642023ca9026e25398050262352d0d71c1840b615","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_cf9be8216996c4d258e271e175dbdfa762d19514a30126e3cded94dcf4248f72","slc_df48e73ad9357e0603a86a6827e0fa7f93bf2cb782a8f632ab60d94cfb501fe0"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"hax is described as a minimalist, terminal-native coding agent implemented as a single native C binary with a small dependency set and low memory use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9b59f4f15688487fb745cb0a2d3d2ba62e878be4b35204e34833b791474440f9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7a2024863e3ebb76065ecbb75c53c0150f52f41553daefff36551a740be297ae"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"Automatic compaction summarizes history near the context limit, triggered by a configurable percentage threshold (default 85), with the context limit overridable per model.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bc9b23f179cc2547507574b6a9ac45cc57bb72cbc7b4a1e7c28673849daa812f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_62e9102d97dd7f8fcbbfcdcfee38184d2ae1471c1089638a394f53113d2ec3ff","slc_f01b8053413936fd8de87c33f390a83d0574b183d8e2565962db341cdcb232e9"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"Settings resolve in order: current-process override, resumed conversation, environment, state.json, config.json, then default; the resumed tier covers provider, model, effort, and preset.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c9d5a1b88cdac4f985913f789a56f9a7e6ca46b6f036521f66d9ef710fe1bc11","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_aba931c7dfc6f07eee9ab901be644cc1c7f771481e29b4b0f025a68c255c59f8","slc_db0f9c8129c6d3a12eb296d0eb1689efdfa0e0cc7421fa0771fa2beffe6b2508"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"hax follows the XDG Base Directory specification: config at ~/.config/hax/config.json, remembered interactive selections and sessions under ~/.local/state/hax/, and a model-metadata cache at ~/.cache/hax/catalog.json.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_defc6b4ab2f30fe75377dab8c4d6c2a1adfd56a0545a2f1f11d41873e00aa16f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb37cc9788c9d5b477d30d972ce0c8861c565b4417eaf5bef9a2528ad2663d4b","slc_cf9be8216996c4d258e271e175dbdfa762d19514a30126e3cded94dcf4248f72"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"The project deliberately omits MCP marketplaces, a plugin runtime, IDE panels, and per-command permission prompts, composing instead via subprocesses and documenting each omission in docs/philosophy.md.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e89eb6ec1c02f1fa6269c0cd31c8271d35076382d550e55de55c8ba5876ede2a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_bb37cc9788c9d5b477d30d972ce0c8861c565b4417eaf5bef9a2528ad2663d4b"],"source_ids":["src_0495887c31cc5dab983967fddfa22b1e"],"text":"By design hax lacks MCP marketplaces, a plugin runtime, IDE panels, and per-command permission prompts; the philosophy doc explains each omission and the pattern covering the need.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","created_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f236947bb815e2739c3fd0f79ebf9a5e98f648719e749328734746913f61a046","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"oleksandrchekhovskyi/hax@7db349773eb7 snapshot bcb987170292241c","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_45ee8ef026ef73ba8d3c9948662eb9eece64c917fdb7000139b55643453fc1ac","slc_db0dd2d77c17bc4105c8b07c4bf1b4758ff03c9967e9aba9542a91199b233770"],"source_ids":["src_afbde6178faf554e82c2127e95c35d59"],"text":"Model metadata (context limits, image capability, estimated spend) is fetched from models.dev and cached, refreshed in the background only when a catalog-identified provider needs it and the cache is stale; fetching can be disabled via catalog.url or catalog.refresh.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:24:52Z","updated_by_operation":"op_16c69f872e334e028dac6d4e82b36467"}
